# Cloudflare Worker Environment Variables & Secrets Reference
# Application: EvolveAI Backend API (workers/api)

## 1. Public Variables (configured in wrangler.toml)

| Variable | Environment | Example / Value | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `ENVIRONMENT` | development | `development` | Target execution environment identifier |
| `ENVIRONMENT` | staging | `staging` | Staging execution environment identifier |
| `ENVIRONMENT` | production | `production` | Production execution environment identifier |
| `CLIENT_ORIGIN` | development | `http://localhost:5173` | Frontend origin permitted by CORS & CSRF middleware |
| `CLIENT_ORIGIN` | staging | `https://staging.evolve-ai.pages.dev` | Staging frontend origin |
| `CLIENT_ORIGIN` | production | `https://evolve-ai.pages.dev` | Production frontend origin |

---

## 2. D1 Database Bindings (configured in wrangler.toml)

| Binding Name | Target Database Name | Environment | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `DB` | `evolve-ai-db` | local/dev | Local SQLite D1 instance |
| `DB` | `evolve-ai-db-staging` | staging | Staging Cloudflare D1 database (isolated from production) |
| `DB` | `evolve-ai-db-production` | production | Production Cloudflare D1 database |

---

## 3. Worker Secrets (MANDATORY: set via `wrangler secret put <NAME> --env <ENV>`)
*NEVER commit actual secret values to git, wrangler.toml, or documentation.*

| Secret Name | Requirements | Description | How to Configure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `ENCRYPTION_SECRET` | Exactly 32 bytes (64-char hex or 44-char base64) | Master encryption key for HKDF-SHA256 & AES-256-GCM credential encryption | `npx wrangler secret put ENCRYPTION_SECRET --env staging` |
| `SESSION_SECRET` | Cryptographically random string (min 32 chars) | HMAC session signature / rotation entropy | `npx wrangler secret put SESSION_SECRET --env staging` |

### How to Generate a Secure 32-Byte Secret Locally:
```bash
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
```
